{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534768-which-mechanics-for-blood-sorcery-you-use","id":1534768,"title":"Which mechanics for Blood Sorcery you use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-26T10:19:32-07:00","id":1534768,"title":"Which mechanics for Blood Sorcery you use?","content":"As the title says. I am a bit curious which mechanics most people use? Core Blood Sorcery, adapted sacrament and blasphemy, Rites of damnation, NMD Requiem for Rome Blood Sorcery? Or something else?<br /> <br /> And why did you pick one over the other?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26883,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","user":"ImortalKiller","date":". 04-26-2024, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T20:15:32-07:00","id":1534792,"title":"","content":"For NPCs in most games I just use vanilla blood sorcery. In games where a PC is interested in going down that path we usually use <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\">Rites of Damnation</a> by Falco. I haven't had a chance to use the new RfR rules yet, but that will probably replace vanilla in the next game I run, at the very least.<br /> <br /> Notable that Rites of Damnation, like Sacraments, is a super heavy way to handle the system, but the complexity pays off for characters that really want to make Blood Sorcery their thing. I probably wouldn't use it in a normal-sized group (mine is small) unless I was confident in the player's ability to run with it without double checking each cast (which is a higher bar than it sounds).<br /> <br /> I've seen concerns about it being unbalancing vs non-blood-sorcerers in mixed games, but I've found that to be a pretty minimal issue in actual play. Each dot of Themes costs just as much as an in-clan Discipline dot, and while yes, they do bring more versatility than a given dot in any discipline, the actual level of power scales <i>slower</i> than Disciplines do, imo. You'd need to play a game with a truly prodigious amount of XP for it to actually end up as an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-28T14:10:52-07:00","id":1534860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1534768-which-mechanics-for-blood-sorcery-you-use?p=1534792#post1534792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For NPCs in most games I just use vanilla blood sorcery. In games where a PC is interested in going down that path we usually use <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/263371/Blood-Sorcery-Rites-of-Damnation\" target=\"_blank\">Rites of Damnation</a> by Falco. I haven't had a chance to use the new RfR rules yet, but that will probably replace vanilla in the next game I run, at the very least.<br /> <br /> Notable that Rites of Damnation, like Sacraments, is a super heavy way to handle the system, but the complexity pays off for characters that really want to make Blood Sorcery their thing. I probably wouldn't use it in a normal-sized group (mine is small) unless I was confident in the player's ability to run with it without double checking each cast (which is a higher bar than it sounds).<br /> <br /> I've seen concerns about it being unbalancing vs non-blood-sorcerers in mixed games, but I've found that to be a pretty minimal issue in actual play. Each dot of Themes costs just as much as an in-clan Discipline dot, and while yes, they do bring more versatility than a given dot in any discipline, the actual level of power scales <i>slower</i> than Disciplines do, imo. You'd need to play a game with a truly prodigious amount of XP for it to actually end up as an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for answering. You touched exactly the points I worried the most about Rites of Damnation, how heavy is in play, and make other players feel underpowered. But good to know is not that bad. I had that feeling, but was afraid of being wrong about it. Now about mechanic complexity, is where worry me the most, in general I play with folks that are quite new to CofD and RPG in general, so every time I consider using it, I get a bit reluctant because of that. But being honest I am a bit anxious for the day some of my players ask to use it haha.<br /> <br /> I am considering, for a game I am planning to run, use NMD System, but create a merit to allow to upgrade their sorcery for Rites of Damnation, but not sure yet.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T09:05:35-07:00","id":1536258,"title":"","content":"I think I am in a similar situation.<br /> <br /> My current plan:<br /> <br /> 1) I will use the book <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies </b>to update the rituals from the 1e books like <b>Circle of the Crone</b> covenant book:<br /> - Target number of successes (<b>BS: S&amp;B</b>)<br /> - Casting time (<b>V:TR 2e</b> core book)<br /> <br /> 2) I will use the mechanics from the <b>V:TR 2e </b>core book, but I might use <b>Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies </b>or <b>Blood Sorcery: Rites of Damnation </b>to create new rituals at some point.<br /> (I won\u2019t give the players the option to create new rituals on the fly. Besides I don\u2019t think they would like to learn that anyway. They are not fond of learning rules\u2026)<br /> <br /> 3) If it feels to slow or something feels off, I might consider the <b>Requiem Errata</b> by None More Dark Publishing<br /> <br /> This plan is based on my current research about the topic, I haven\u2019t read the books yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 05-25-2024, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}